  ! Use Math.trunc() instead of parseInt(String(...), 10).
  
    1 │ /* should generate diagnostics */
  > 2 │ const a = parseInt(String(number as number), 10);
      │           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ const b = parseInt(String<() => number>(number), 10);
    4 │ const c = parseInt(String(number!), 10);
  
  i Very large and very small numbers turn into strings such as "1e+21", which parseInt() reads as 1.
  
  i Math.trunc() removes the decimal part of any number and states the intent clearly.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  
  i Unsafe fix: Use Math.trunc() instead.
  
